q('Photosynthesis removes atmospheric CO2 when:',['plants take in CO2 and form organic matter','combustion occurs','respiration occurs','denitrification occurs'],0,['Correct.','Combustion releases CO2.','Respiration releases CO2.','Denitrification is nitrogen cycling.']),
q('In the fast carbon cycle, CO2 returns to the atmosphere through:',['respiration and decomposition','only fossilisation','only shell formation','nitrogen fixation'],0,['Correct.','Fossilisation is slow storage.','Shells store carbon.','Nitrogen fixation concerns nitrogen.']),
q('Ammonia → nitrite → nitrate is called:',['Nitrification','Denitrification','Assimilation','Photosynthesis'],0,['Correct.','Denitrification returns some nitrate to N2.','Assimilation is uptake.','Photosynthesis is a different process.']),
